{"The bulk update with empty data object will not actually update updatedAt as intended - should pass updatedAt: new Date() to ensure the timestamp is refreshed": 0.8898427486419678, "Updating the .env file uses sed -i '' which only works on BSD sed - on GNU/Linux environments sed interprets '' as a filename and aborts with 'No such file or directory'": 0.949733555316925, "Throwing a generic Error when the credential is not found will be surfaced by tRPC as an internal server error instead of a structured not-found/authorization error - should use TRPCError with code NOT_FOUND": 0.7449939846992493, "The mock implementation of getCacheStatusByCredentialIds does not accept any parameters and returns a plain array, which is incompatible with the ICalendarCacheRepository interface that expects a credential ID list parameter and a typed result": 0.7774748206138611, "When a user has no connected calendars, credentialIds becomes an empty array, and passing it to Prisma's in filter causes prisma.calendarCache.groupBy to throw 'An empty list is not allowed for in filters'": 0.9485817551612854}